                            Constitutional law<br/>
                    </span>
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    Applied: R. v. Jordan, <b>2016 SCC 27</b>, [2016] 1 S.C.R. 631; referred to: R. v. Cody, 2017 SCC 31, [2017] 1 S.C.R. 659; R. v. Morin, [1992] 1 S.C.R. 771; R. v. Williamson, 2016 SCC 28, [2016] 1 S.C.R. 741. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[1] The Court — The bulk of this case occurred before the release of this Court’s decision in R. v. Jordan, <b>2016 SCC 27</b>, [2016] 1 S.C.R. 631. The facts leading to the respondent’s s. 11(b) challenge are indicative of the culture of rampant and long-standing systemic delay — and complacency towards that delay — that had 
