                     (7th) 31; R. v. Morris, 2013 ONCA 223, 305 O.A.C. 47; R. v. Campbell, 2017 ONSC 26; R. v. Bonneteau, 2016 MBCA 72, 330 Man. R. (2d) 139; R. v. Jordan, <b>2016 SCC 27</b>, [2016] 1 S.C.R. 631; R. v. Askov, [1990] 2 S.C.R. 1199; R. v. Codina #1, 2017 ONSC 7162, 56 Imm. L.R. (4th) 43; R. v. Codina, 2017 ONSC 7315, 408 C.R.R. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;While Moldaver J.’s observations in R. v. Jordan, <b>2016 SCC 27</b>, [2016] 1 S.C.R. 631, relate to the impact of delays on s. 11(b) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms, I find them apt in this context as well. 
                </p>
                <div class="spacer">
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                </div>
        </div> 
        <div class="documents">
